Mg is a Micro (GNU) Emacs: small, fast, portable Emacs-like editor,
public domain, created 1987 from MicroEMACS v30.

This is the troglobit fork, tracking OpenBSD mg upstream and adding new
usability features: UTF-8 (multibyte type/display/edit, Unicode 17),
syntax highlighting with file modes (c, markdown, yaml, python, ...),
quick help C-h q with a built-in tutorial, M-; comment-dwim, line
numbers, buffer cycling C-x Left/Right, ido-style prompts.

Replaces the stock editors/mg (PORTEPOCH=2 wins over dated snapshots).
WWW: https://github.com/troglobit/mg
